# AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST, and that is the whole point of the file.
#
# The build context is the WORKING TREE, and .gitignore has no say in it. Under a denylist a new
# directory joins the context the day it is created, invisible in `git status` and unmentioned in any
# review: 67MB of assets/baked and assets/gen shipped to the daemon on every build for months that
# way. A denylist fails open, which for a build context means it fails silently and expensively.
#
# So: ignore EVERYTHING, then name what the two Dockerfiles actually COPY. A new directory is now
# absent from the context until somebody says otherwise, and the failure mode of forgetting is a build
# that stops with "not found" instead of one that quietly grows.
#
#   Dockerfile      (the site + docs apps) — themes core formats/scene assets/{icons,vendor,brands,plinth}
#                   scripts site docs-site docker-start.sh
#   Dockerfile.cli  (the renderer)         — go.mod go.sum cmd internal cli core blocks blueprints
#                   themes assets/vendor scripts/{author,media} formats/scene CREDITS.md LICENSE-FAQ.md
#
# EDITING THIS FILE: add a COPY, add its `!` line here in the same commit. `make docker-check` builds
# the context and prints what is in it.

**

# ── the engine, shared by both images ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!core
!themes
!blocks
!blueprints
!cli
# The whole scene directory, not just the page: scene.html loads scene.js and scene.css, and shipping
# only the page put a dead engine in production behind a 200.
!formats/scene
# The site COPYs scripts/ whole (site-engine.mjs vendors the engine into public/); the CLI image takes
# expand-blocks.mjs out of it. One negation covers both.
!scripts
# generators/ bakes the standing assets. Both images RUN generators/media/fonts.mjs to fetch the
# faces, so the directory has to survive the `**` above or COPY fails at build and nowhere else.
!generators

# ── the Go renderer (Dockerfile.cli builder stage) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal

# ── the two web apps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs-site runs on 3001 inside the SAME image and the site rewrites /docs to it. Its .source must
# stay out so the image regenerates it from content/ rather than shipping a stale copy.
!site
!docs-site
!docker-start.sh
!CREDITS.md
!LICENSE-FAQ.md
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.source
# generated by scripts/site/site-engine.mjs during the build (never ship a stale copy)
site/public/core
site/public/themes
site/public/engine
site/public/formats
site/public/scripts

# ── assets: the browser reaches for a handful of real files out of 59M ───────────────────────────
!assets/icons
!assets/vendor
# blocks/geo.mjs imports these at module scope, so without them the whole block registry throws on
# load and /playground shows generators only. 204K.
!assets/geo
# The marks the PUBLISHED scenes name. scripts/site/site-engine.mjs derives this list from the scenes
# themselves and FAILS the build when one is absent — but it looks in the build CONTEXT, and this file
# decides what is in it. So an asset can exist in the repo, pass every local run, and simply not be in
# the image (docs/MISTAKES.md #289). Add a scene that names a new mark, add its line here.
!assets/brands/preface/agents
!assets/brands/argus/mascot.png
!assets/brands/linear/icon.png
!assets/brands/looks/photos/michelangelo-david-sculpture-head-2.webp
!assets/brands/ditherkit/sections/03-area.png
!assets/brands/ditherkit/sections/04-bar.png
!assets/brands/ditherkit/sections/05-line.png
!assets/brands/threadcite/components/howitworks.json
!assets/brands/threadcite/icon.svg
# plinth sits outside assets/brands and one published scene reaches for its hero figure.
!assets/plinth/hero-figure.png
